Infected port: a bounded wait for the garbage collector after a failed GPU allocation (vglSetGcPauseMs), and counters (vglGetStats).
When a GPU allocation failed, the unsafe allocators asked the garbage collector for a cycle and then slept sceKernelDelayThread(1000000), a full second, once per attempt and up to four attempts: a freeze of one to four seconds the first time memory ran out. With a limit in milliseconds the allocator looks at the collector's pull semaphore every millisecond and leaves as soon as the cycle has given its slot back, or when the limit is up. 0 (the default) keeps the second.
vglGetStats returns counts of shader cache hits, shader compiles and compile failures, allocation failures and GC pauses (count, total and longest, in microseconds). NO_DEBUG builds have no log, so the port reads these.

